B.ce(1, (12, 32, 36),
     '15-4-112, Patamata,\nVijayawada.\n10th March, 2027.\n\nDear Kalyan,\n'
     'I am fine here and hope you are fine too. I want to share a small experience that gave me great happiness.\n'
     'Last month heavy rains flooded the low-lying colony near our school. Many poor families lost their food grains, clothes and books. '
     'Our class decided to help them. We collected old clothes, rice, dal and notebooks from our neighbours. I gave my pocket money of ₹500 that I had saved for a new cricket bat. '
     'On Sunday, with our teacher, we distributed the packets to forty families. I also spent two evenings teaching small children whose books were washed away.\n'
     'When an old woman blessed me with tears in her eyes, I remembered the postmaster in “A Letter to God” who helped Lencho. I understood that helping others in cash, kind or service is the real worship of God.\n'
     'Do you also help others in your area? Write to me about it. Convey my regards to your parents.\n\n'
     'Yours lovingly,\nVarun.\n\nAddress on the envelope:\nTo\nK. Kalyan,\nD.No. 4-12, Brodipet,\nGuntur.')
B.ce(1, (12, 37, 39),
     'Helping the Needy – Speech\n'
     'Respected Headmaster, teachers and my dear friends, good morning.\n'
     'Today I would like to speak on “Helping the Needy”.\n'
     'Our elders say, “Service to man is service to God.” God is none other than the person who helps us in our hard times. In “A Letter to God”, the postmaster and his employees became God for Lencho by sending him money.\n'
     'Mother Teresa served the poor and the sick all her life. Swami Vivekananda said that serving the poor is serving God.\n'
     'We students can also help others: we can share our books and clothes, teach weaker classmates, donate blood when we grow up, help old people cross the road, and give food to the hungry. Even a kind word and a smile are help.\n'
     'Helping others does not need riches; it needs a kind heart. When we help others, we get peace and happiness.\n'
     'So, let us all promise today to help at least one needy person every week.\nThank you.')

