     'Speech on International Day of Yoga (21st June)\n'
     'Respected Headmaster, teachers and dear friends, good morning.\n'
     'Today we celebrate the International Day of Yoga. I am happy to speak a few words on Yoga.\n'
     '• India is the birthplace of Yoga. Our sage Patanjali gave us the “Yoga Sutras” thousands of years ago. In 2014 the United Nations declared 21st June as the International Day of Yoga, and now the whole world practises it.\n'
     '• Yoga is not just exercise. It unites the body, the mind and the breath through asanas, pranayama and meditation.\n'
     '• Physical benefits: it makes the body flexible and strong, improves blood circulation, digestion and immunity, and helps control weight, BP and diabetes.\n'
     '• Mental benefits: it reduces stress and anger, improves concentration and memory – very useful for us students during exams – and gives peace of mind.\n'
     '• We should make Yoga a part of our daily routine. Even 20 minutes every morning – Surya Namaskar, a few asanas and deep breathing – can keep us healthy and happy.\n'
